In article <1992Mar20.022423.9658@reed.edu> 
nelson@reed.edu (Nelson Minar) writes:
>Does anyone know exactly how long the prayer timeout is? It seems to
>be roughly every 1000 turns, and can be shortened by sacrificing. But
>I have gotten away with praying every 800 turns or so when I've
>needed.
  
  The timeout is random, and it has a pretty strange distribution.
Its median value is about 350 turns, but it has a substantial
probability of being either very short or very long (i.e.
thousands of turns).  You can get away with praying every
800 turns for a while, but sooner or later you'll get
burned.

  When you have Hand of Elbereth, the median goes up to 1000
turns.

  Sacrificing shortens the timeout.  If you sacrifice and you
don't get the message "You have a hopeful feeling," then it
is safe to pray.

